### LinkedIn Post 2: Engineering Insights (2026-03-18 14:00 KST)

```
HTTP/1.1 in 320 Lines of Code

When we implemented HTTP from scratch in FreeLang, we learned:

✅ The protocol is more logical than magical
✅ Performance bottlenecks are predictable (file I/O, JSON parsing)
✅ Caching impact is massive (22x improvement!)
✅ Security is a choice, not an afterthought

Key Insights:
- Request parsing: Parse line → extract method/path → headers → body
- Response generation: Structure data → serialize → send
- Caching: O(1) lookup with TTL beats repeated processing every time

For engineering teams rebuilding systems, this architecture shows:
- Where optimization matters most
- How to implement each layer independently
- Why understanding fundamentals beats framework expertise

The code is fully open-source and documented.

